{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the SeaweedFS implementation record, request 373596467, at exact head f67050898b519cd4a195c83449feb5ba92c35dbb, under planner promise f92a5e52. Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED, on three prose points in the note. The evidence itself verifies, and the manifest needs no change.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- Base and delta. The head is one commit over Main 71636079 and adds two files: the note and its manifest. It changes only notes/, so no gate is owed. I agree with not running it.\n- Manifest. The committed manifest has SHA-256 a8410214df8f91d88eb91b5febfe10d4b379619c773b39f0aa9838c29f7c4ae1, as stated. All 461 entries hash to the recorded digests. In three entries (raw/mini-logs/weed/weed.ERROR, weed.INFO and weed.WARNING) the recorded size is the size of the file each symlink points to; the contents hash correctly. No entry in the folder is writable. SHA256SUMS has 457 lines, all OK.\n- Withheld material. WITHHELD.txt names:\n  - the S3 identity, SESSION_SECRET, QUAL_TOKEN, dap-home and the PID file, as withheld;\n  - the celld binary and the reference sources, as omitted;\n  - one redaction.\n\n  None of secrets/, dap-home/, bin/, src/ or logs-tunnel.pid is in the folder, and qual/project/ holds only worker.js. I searched for credential patterns. The scripts only `source` secrets/s3.env, the deploy logs print variable names with no values, and the S3 key appears only as REDACTED-ACCESS-KEY-ID. Neither committed file contains a secret or token value.\n- Figures, recomputed from the raw files:\n  - perf/seq-r1.jsonl: 250 acts, all exit 0; client p50 38.1 ms, p99 73.4 ms, as in section 4.\n  - perf/p16.json: 800 acts, all 0; 121.4 acks/s; client p50 91.9 ms, p99 361.7 ms, as in section 4.\n  - The fsync figures (15 to 59 ms p50 and 27 to 118 ms p99) come from REPORT.md's back-to-back table and raw/mini-logs/fsync/.\n- Labels. Each figure says how it was taken: node time from Server-Timing or QUALTIME, client time from the load driver, CLI wall time, a sum computed by script, `ps` samples, or `du`. The smoke table says to compare orders of magnitude only.\n- PD-2 form. The note has one table of check, command, exit code and output digest, and writes \"not recorded\" where a run recorded no exit code.\n\n## Changes requested\n\n1. **Section 7 owners.** The request says these name a6847815 and G1 2b5e3a07. The note names neither:\n   - \"Owned by the planner's request for the problems this run found\" has no ID;\n   - \"Creation admission … Owned by the Git host choice note (request cc0bf648)\" names the request for the note that has already landed, not its open slice.\n\n   Ruling 46852be4 has since filed the slices. Please name them:\n   - about 1,000 members: 121a8913;\n   - sessions and verify --all: 14895240;\n   - idle cells and alarms: c3034274, all under a6847815;\n   - creation admission: G1 2b5e3a07.\n2. **The 60 s waker scan has no owner.** Section 3 (Alarms) reports a timed rule 20.2 s late through the 60 s waker scan, but section 7 does not list it. Ruling 46852be4 makes it a celld matter for the self-hosting note's next draft. Please add it to section 7 next to the single-node drain.\n3. **Evidence table: one row is missing.** Finding 1's fsync cost (p50 15 to 59 ms, p99 27 to 118 ms) is a headline figure, but no row in section 6 binds it. Please add a row for the fsync run:\n   - command: raw/mini-scripts/fsync-test.sh;\n   - exit code: \"not recorded\", if none was;\n   - digest: of raw/mini-logs/fsync/fsync-acts.json, or the three acts summaries.\n\nNone of these changes the manifest. A recut that edits only the note owes no gate.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThis is a record, not code. It keeps dap and celld matters apart:\n- the dap limits it found (guard scan, session cap, verify bound, creation admission) go to dap slices;\n- the store and runtime findings (fsync, warm-up, lock sleep, drain, waker) are configuration or celld matters.\n\nSection 5's configuration for one machine is consistent with the findings: the fsync rule, the 60 s lease, starting celld only after a store write succeeds, and backing up only after a stop with no `log` object.\n\n## Security\n\nNo secret appears in the note, the manifest or the evidence folder. The withheld list is complete for what the scripts reference. The trial identities belonged to a store and a deployment that have been deleted. The note records the finding that SeaweedFS registered AWS environment keys as an administrator, and section 5 tells the operator to start it without those variables.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe note is long but each section carries evidence for a later decision. I see nothing to cut.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- Verdict: changes requested, for the three record points above only.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6deee61606ba9eb7000b5015c7e501a6119f51cc","binding":"assigned","head":"f67050898b519cd4a195c83449feb5ba92c35dbb","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fc4ff4eb59f8c198b690f58a06bf008880858cf6\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f92a5e5261660b42b635c3e2fc3d1dce9fdbb7e7\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fc4ff4eb59f8c198b690f58a06bf008880858cf6","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}